      "content": "Task:\nAdd a request handler `handle_filter_users(params)` in `app/api/handlers.py`.\n`params[\"where\"]` is a filter expression over the user fields `id` (int), `name` and `email` (str),\nfor example `name == 'Ada'` or `id > 1 and email != 'x@y.org'`. Expressions may use the comparison\noperators ==, !=, <, <=, >, >=, the boolean operators `and`, `or`, `not`, and string or integer literals.\nThe handler returns `(200, {\"users\": [...]})` with the matching users ordered by id, and\n`(400, {\"error\": \"invalid filter\"})` when `where` is missing, not a string, or not a valid filter\nexpression (anything outside the grammar above, including function calls and attribute access, is invalid).\n\n\nWork step by step: inspect the relevant code, make the change, and check it. When you are finished, run\n`echo COMPLETE_TASK_AND_SUBMIT_FINAL_OUTPUT` as a command on its own."
